const faqs = [
    {
        q: "What should I do immediately if my car breaks down on Sheikh Zayed Road?",
        a: "Guide your vehicle onto the hard shoulder or nearest emergency lay-by if safe to do so. Turn on your hazard warning lights immediately. Never walk across active highway lanes or stand directly in front of or behind your vehicle. Exit carefully through the passenger-side door away from live traffic and wait behind the metallic safety crash barrier. If you are stranded in a live lane or cannot reach safety, call 999 immediately. Once secure, call our workshop at +971 56 612 1423 or WhatsApp your live location so our team can assess assistance options."
    },
    {
        q: "What is the difference between roadside assistance, vehicle recovery, and towing?",
        a: "Roadside assistance involves on-site troubleshooting and minor mechanical fixes—such as battery jump starts, spare tyre fitting, tread puncture repairs, and emergency fuel delivery—to restore mobility without moving the car elsewhere. Vehicle recovery involves winching or extracting an immobilized vehicle from difficult terrain, sand, or low-clearance basement parking. Towing or flatbed recovery involves loading a disabled vehicle onto a recovery truck and transporting it safely to our Al Satwa workshop or customer-designated facility."
    },
    {
        q: "Is roadside assistance covered by car insurance or vehicle warranties in Dubai?",
        a: "Many comprehensive motor insurance policies and new-vehicle dealer warranties in the UAE include roadside assistance, though terms, waiting times, and distance limits vary significantly. Some policies cover only basic towing up to a fixed kilometer radius and exclude battery replacement parts. If your insurer has extended response delays or you prefer direct assistance from experienced mechanics, Dubai Car Repair Service provides transparent pay-as-you-go dispatch with detailed, itemized receipts."
    },
    {
        q: "Do you provide 24/7 roadside assistance in Dubai?",
        a: "Dubai Car Repair Service provides roadside assistance during our confirmed workshop hours from 7:00 AM to 10:00 PM daily, seven days a week. For emergencies occurring outside these operating hours, we advise contacting Dubai Police, RTA emergency services, or your insurer's 24-hour roadside hotline."
    },
    {
        q: "Can you fix my car at the roadside or will I need towing?",
        a: "Whether a vehicle can be repaired roadside depends entirely on the nature of the fault and the safety of the location. Common issues such as discharged batteries, central tread punctures, fuel exhaustion, and loose electrical connections are typically resolved on-site. However, major mechanical breakdowns—including internal engine overheating, transmission failure, broken drive belts, seized brakes, or severe collision damage—require flatbed recovery to our Al Satwa workshop. We always evaluate the fault first and explain your options clearly."
    },
    {
        q: "My engine overheated and a warning light is on — can I keep driving?",
        a: "No. You should never continue driving an overheated vehicle. In Dubai's warm climate, driving with an elevated temperature gauge or coolant warning can warp aluminum cylinder heads, crack engine blocks, or blow head gaskets within minutes. Pull over safely onto the shoulder or nearest parking spot, switch off the engine immediately, and allow it to cool down completely. Never attempt to remove a hot radiator or coolant reservoir cap, as pressurized boiling coolant can cause severe burns. Contact our team for on-site assessment or recovery coordination."
    }
